{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('PROGRESS.md')\ns=p.read_text().replace('## Current status\\\\nRead TASK.md and all PLAN.md sections. Implementing','## Current status\\\\nCore implementation assembled; first build and browser verification starting. Implemented')\ns=s.replace('1. Scaffold/build and procedural world/simulation.\\\\n2. Gameplay, campaign, UI and audio.\\\\n3. Attract, multiplayer, dev tools.\\\\n4. Tests, screenshots, fixes.\\\\n5. Final metadata, build, exit interview and report.','1. Run first browser build; fix rendering/runtime issues.\\\\n2. Add complete automated sim playthrough, UI, audio, multiplayer and viewport checks.\\\\n3. Verify all campaign interactions and feature coverage; fill missing mechanics.\\\\n4. Inspect screenshots and polish.\\\\n5. Final metadata, final build, exit interview, cleanup and report.\\\\n\\\\n## Implemented files\\\\nDev folder contains modular \"'`src/`: deterministic sim and fire, terrain, Rapier wrapper, all contract/world/weapon data, 3D procedural renderer + TSL ink post, skeletal animation, 10-foot UI, keyboard/mouse/controller input, procedural audio, 14-vignette attract, AI Hub and BroadcastChannel networking. `tools/build.mjs` bundles all dependencies/fonts into the root HTML and writes exit interview from about.json. Dependencies installed locally.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Known areas needing verification\\\\n- First runtime rendering, interaction conflicts, exact bot completion and feature coverage have not yet been checked.\\\\n- Physics driving currently uses authored bicycle motion alongside Rapier raycast suspension.\\\\n- Network remote avatars, buddy/AI job partner, some debug overlays and world ambience need a completion pass.\\\\n- About feedback currently uses unknown until tests complete.\\\\n')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('PROGRESS.md')\ns=p.read_text().replace('## Current status\\\\nRead TASK.md and all PLAN.md sections. Implementing','## Current status\\\\nCore implementation assembled; first build and browser verification starting. Implemented')\ns=s.replace('1. Scaffold/build and procedural world/simulation.\\\\n2. Gameplay, campaign, UI and audio.\\\\n3. Attract, multiplayer, dev tools.\\\\n4. Tests, screenshots, fixes.\\\\n5. Final metadata, build, exit interview and report.','1. Run first browser build; fix rendering/runtime issues.\\\\n2. Add complete automated sim playthrough, UI, audio, multiplayer and viewport checks.\\\\n3. Verify all campaign interactions and feature coverage; fill missing mechanics.\\\\n4. Inspect screenshots and polish.\\\\n5. Final metadata, final build, exit interview, cleanup and report.\\\\n\\\\n## Implemented files\\\\nDev folder contains modular \"'`src/`: deterministic sim and fire, terrain, Rapier wrapper, all contract/world/weapon data, 3D procedural renderer + TSL ink post, skeletal animation, 10-foot UI, keyboard/mouse/controller input, procedural audio, 14-vignette attract, AI Hub and BroadcastChannel networking. `tools/build.mjs` bundles all dependencies/fonts into the root HTML and writes exit interview from about.json. Dependencies installed locally.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Known areas needing verification\\\\n- First runtime rendering, interaction conflicts, exact bot completion and feature coverage have not yet been checked.\\\\n- Physics driving currently uses authored bicycle motion alongside Rapier raycast suspension.\\\\n- Network remote avatars, buddy/AI job partner, some debug overlays and world ambience need a completion pass.\\\\n- About feedback currently uses unknown until tests complete.\\\\n')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The first single-file build is ready, with the engine, physics, fonts, and audio code bundled inside it. I’m starting browser verification now, then I’ll test the campaign and multiplayer. The main risks to check are interaction conflicts and whether graphics startup leaves the co-op protocol responsive.\n"}}
