{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/data/about.json');a=json.loads(p.read_text());a['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless scripted simulation and complete campaign through all three endings; Playwright 1.63.0; virtual standard gamepad, touch profiles and offline audio; Chromium WebGPU/WebGL2, WebKit and Firefox; 24 viewport combinations; official Hub harness and two-player co-op. No physical controller or real iOS hardware.'\na['sourceInformation']['research']='Provided PLAN.md and TASK.md; official AI Hub Session Protocol v1 README, client 1.4.0 and harness; local Three.js source and installed testing-toolkit help.'\na['testingFeedback']=['16 gameplay or presentation issues found and corrected. Concurrent viewport capture and shared-machine memory failures were handled separately by serializing checks and reducing session graphics load.','4 game-breaking issues: movement after skipping the opening, unrelated cargo failing a contract, graphics starving session results, and an uninitialized held-map texture on WebGPU.','The input-driven complete campaign, including twists, both bark errands, a failed cargo retry and all three endings; it exposed interactions that isolated system checks missed.','The title-only smoke check was least informative about gameplay; it could not expose bugs that required a mission or a physical-map interaction.']\na['engineFeedback']=['The same TSL cel and ink pipeline works on WebGPU and the WebGL2 fallback.','Yes. Canvas textures need an initialized rendering context before WebGPU upload, and expensive software frames can delay multiplayer messages.','The seeded simulation connecting fire, survival, weapons, vehicles, contracts, world consequences and co-op.','Keeping graphics construction and software rendering from blocking the session protocol.','None. The engine packages are unmodified; shaders, procedural assets and gameplay are application code.','A lighter explicit renderer-start phase and clearer cross-backend diagnostics for canvas textures and multiple render targets.']\na['promptFeedback']=['The original setting, interacting systems and verified rendering recipes gave the game a clear identity.','The boundary between a vertical slice and the complete campaign was unusually broad.','Making the many survival, story and multiplayer systems work together through an entire campaign.','Use one machine-readable acceptance list shared by the plan, task and feature-coverage tests.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('docs/issues-log.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Verified so far:', '''9. Holding Use through the end of the opening immediately opened the Ferryman menu. Added a release gate so the skip gesture cannot become a world interaction.\n10. Synthetic mouse events following touch could rebuild the title menu during a tap. Mouse, keyboard and touch input now have separate unlock rules; Android and WebKit tap checks pass.\n11. The objective accumulator discarded a fractional step and made timed endings run long. Fixed by retaining the remainder.\n12. Saving immediately before an ending choice lost the pending choice on reload. Pending choices are now preserved and reconstructed.\n13. **Critical:** expensive session graphics could delay first traffic or a result beyond the Hub grace period. Initial traffic now precedes graphics, static scenery is batched, expensive frames are governed, and fallback session graphics use a smaller allocation.\n14. **Critical:** the physical held map uploaded a canvas before it had a Canvas2D context, stopping WebGPU rendering. The map is drawn before its GPU texture can become visible.\n15. Night skies changed while constant ambient light left the ground too bright. Ambient light and the ink grade now follow the night factor.\n16. Two-sided sign planes showed mirrored text from behind. Signs now have correctly oriented front and back faces.\n\nAdditional implementation corrections during code inspection: vehicle steering direction and handbrake; controller vehicle look/lights; player-specific case restrictions, case drop replication and group extraction; visible driving map; restored broken guns from an armoury; dev overlays and placed prefabs.\n\nTesting tally: 16 confirmed product issues, including 4 game-breaking issues. No unresolved product issue is listed here. Environmental capture or memory failures and test harness corrections are not included in that tally.\n\nVerified so far:''')\ns += '\\\\nFinal reports are recorded in \"'`test-output/last-results.json`, `feature-coverage.json`, `attract-coverage.json`, the Hub reports and the serialized viewport reports.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/tests/sim.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"import {createSim}\\\",\\\"import {validate} from '../validate-data.mjs';\\\\nimport {createSim}\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"c.assert(PLACES.length>=20);\\\", \\\"c.equal(validate(),[]);c.assert(PLACES.length>=20);\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/tests/ui.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"length:18},(_,i)=>['about'\\\", \\\"length:19},(_,i)=>['about'\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/data/about.json');a=json.loads(p.read_text());a['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless scripted simulation and complete campaign through all three endings; Playwright 1.63.0; virtual standard gamepad, touch profiles and offline audio; Chromium WebGPU/WebGL2, WebKit and Firefox; 24 viewport combinations; official Hub harness and two-player co-op. No physical controller or real iOS hardware.'\na['sourceInformation']['research']='Provided PLAN.md and TASK.md; official AI Hub Session Protocol v1 README, client 1.4.0 and harness; local Three.js source and installed testing-toolkit help.'\na['testingFeedback']=['16 gameplay or presentation issues found and corrected. Concurrent viewport capture and shared-machine memory failures were handled separately by serializing checks and reducing session graphics load.','4 game-breaking issues: movement after skipping the opening, unrelated cargo failing a contract, graphics starving session results, and an uninitialized held-map texture on WebGPU.','The input-driven complete campaign, including twists, both bark errands, a failed cargo retry and all three endings; it exposed interactions that isolated system checks missed.','The title-only smoke check was least informative about gameplay; it could not expose bugs that required a mission or a physical-map interaction.']\na['engineFeedback']=['The same TSL cel and ink pipeline works on WebGPU and the WebGL2 fallback.','Yes. Canvas textures need an initialized rendering context before WebGPU upload, and expensive software frames can delay multiplayer messages.','The seeded simulation connecting fire, survival, weapons, vehicles, contracts, world consequences and co-op.','Keeping graphics construction and software rendering from blocking the session protocol.','None. The engine packages are unmodified; shaders, procedural assets and gameplay are application code.','A lighter explicit renderer-start phase and clearer cross-backend diagnostics for canvas textures and multiple render targets.']\na['promptFeedback']=['The original setting, interacting systems and verified rendering recipes gave the game a clear identity.','The boundary between a vertical slice and the complete campaign was unusually broad.','Making the many survival, story and multiplayer systems work together through an entire campaign.','Use one machine-readable acceptance list shared by the plan, task and feature-coverage tests.']\np.write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('docs/issues-log.md');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('Verified so far:', '''9. Holding Use through the end of the opening immediately opened the Ferryman menu. Added a release gate so the skip gesture cannot become a world interaction.\n10. Synthetic mouse events following touch could rebuild the title menu during a tap. Mouse, keyboard and touch input now have separate unlock rules; Android and WebKit tap checks pass.\n11. The objective accumulator discarded a fractional step and made timed endings run long. Fixed by retaining the remainder.\n12. Saving immediately before an ending choice lost the pending choice on reload. Pending choices are now preserved and reconstructed.\n13. **Critical:** expensive session graphics could delay first traffic or a result beyond the Hub grace period. Initial traffic now precedes graphics, static scenery is batched, expensive frames are governed, and fallback session graphics use a smaller allocation.\n14. **Critical:** the physical held map uploaded a canvas before it had a Canvas2D context, stopping WebGPU rendering. The map is drawn before its GPU texture can become visible.\n15. Night skies changed while constant ambient light left the ground too bright. Ambient light and the ink grade now follow the night factor.\n16. Two-sided sign planes showed mirrored text from behind. Signs now have correctly oriented front and back faces.\n\nAdditional implementation corrections during code inspection: vehicle steering direction and handbrake; controller vehicle look/lights; player-specific case restrictions, case drop replication and group extraction; visible driving map; restored broken guns from an armoury; dev overlays and placed prefabs.\n\nTesting tally: 16 confirmed product issues, including 4 game-breaking issues. No unresolved product issue is listed here. Environmental capture or memory failures and test harness corrections are not included in that tally.\n\nVerified so far:''')\ns += '\\\\nFinal reports are recorded in \"'`test-output/last-results.json`, `feature-coverage.json`, `attract-coverage.json`, the Hub reports and the serialized viewport reports.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/tests/sim.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"import {createSim}\\\",\\\"import {validate} from '../validate-data.mjs';\\\\nimport {createSim}\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"c.assert(PLACES.length>=20);\\\", \\\"c.equal(validate(),[]);c.assert(PLACES.length>=20);\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('tools/tests/ui.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"length:18},(_,i)=>['about'\\\", \\\"length:19},(_,i)=>['about'\\\");p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
