{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_123","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/data/about.json');a=json.loads(p.read_text());a['testingFeedback'][0]=a['testingFeedback'][0].replace('16 gameplay','17 gameplay');p.write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('docs/issues-log.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Testing tally: 16 confirmed', '17. Short desktop and landscape title layouts clipped menu items or overlapped the footer. Added a compact title rule for viewports below 600 pixels high.\\\\n\\\\nTesting tally: 17 confirmed');s+='\\\\nA combined in-process test run retained the large simulation heap while launching browsers, triggering shared-machine memory kills. The single test command now isolates tiers in child processes and gives each Hub case a fresh page/context. The viewport tool is wrapped without modification to use one engine and page at a time. All 24 serialized viewport captures completed cleanly, including visible WebKit scenes.\\\\n';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/DESIGNER.md');s=p.read_text().replace('The test runner prints failures and one count.', 'The test runner prints failures and one count. Full runs isolate each tier in its own process to release the simulation heap before browser tests; viewport captures use one engine and page at a time.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('../PROGRESS.md');s=p.read_text();s += '''\\\\n## Final verification iteration\\\\n- Expanded Hub suite passed 9/9, including real co-op, same-computer results, and default four-copy WebGL2.\\\\n- Serialized native viewport matrix passed all 24 combinations, no overflow/console/page/request issues. Personally inspected WebKit iPhone SE, iPad, 21:9, landscape, and Chromium tablet images; scenes render.\\\\n- Compact-height title CSS fixed a visual menu/footer overlap.\\\\n- Full in-process suite then ran out of shared RAM because Node retained simulation heap while browsers launched. Runner now uses separate tier child processes and fresh Hub pages; rerunning combined command. Environmental crashes are tracked separately from 17 confirmed product issues (4 critical), all corrected.\\\\n- About/exit interview feedback is filled from the issue log. Latest build includes it.\\\\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet && node tools/test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
