{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_189","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../PROGRESS.md');p.write_text('''# Fare Cry — progress\n\n## Deliverables\n- HTML: \"'`Fare-Cry-Far-Cry-2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-075003.html` in the workspace root.\n- Interview: `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML.\n- Source: `Fare-Cry-Far-Cry-2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-075003/`.\n- Build metadata, feedback and catalogue values come from `src/data/about.json`.\n\n## Completed\n- Original first-person Concession Fourteen campaign: C1–C8, E1/E2, buddy twists, mercy and three endings.\n- Deterministic world/fire/wind, weapons and jams, healing/surgery, fever, rescues, factions, posts/supply, vehicles/repair, boats/ferry, map/GPS/locator, shop, sleep and saves.\n- Three r180 WebGPU/TSL ink/cel rendering with WebGL2 fallback, procedural models, skeletal animation, code-generated audio (music defaults to 10%).\n- Controller/keyboard/mouse UI, PS/Xbox glyphs, live dev tools/sliders, touch-only notice/settings and 14-vignette attract.\n- AI Hub Protocol v1 and same-computer co-op; normal client input, shared case/fire, revives, results and packet budgets exercised.\n- Engine/font licence notices copied under vendor/licenses and embedded in the single HTML. Original Hub client retained byte-for-byte as the first script.\n- Designer docs, validators, balance tool, tests and screenshots.\n\n## Verification\n- Earlier full runs passed 38, then 40, then 41 checks as stronger checks were added.\n- Current final suite target: 42 checks (sim 16, UI 16, Hub 9, viewport matrix 1 covering 24 combinations).\n- Current final build/test command is running in the latest exec session (returned immediately before this log rewrite). Poll it before starting any browser. All older test sessions are finished; an explicit own-workspace process check found no leftovers before this final command.\n- Actual feature coverage: 66/66. Attract coverage has passed ≥80% (about 86%).\n- Personally inspected title, daytime/fire/night, map/surgery/mercy and native phone/tablet/landscape/ultrawide screenshots. The warmed driving capture confirms clear forward view, ring steering wheel and handheld map.\n- Product issue tally in docs/issues-log.md: 24 corrected issues, 7 critical. Shared-machine memory kills and test-infrastructure corrections are logged separately.\n\n## Test resources\n- One browser at a time. Full test tiers are separate child processes to release simulation heap.\n- Hub cases use fresh browsers and wait for available RAM; the unmodified official harness is used.\n- Viewport toolkit is wrapped without changing its installed file to serialize native engines/pages.\n- All local servers are OS-selected 127.0.0.1 ports and close automatically. No persistent dev server.\n\n## Remaining hand-in steps\n1. Wait for the current final full test command; fix only an actual failed required check.\n2. Inspect the final result JSON and final source/HTML/interview consistency; original first script must match vendor/session.js.\n3. Run the warmed driving helper only if a final visual refresh is needed, after the test browser closes.\n4. Remove node_modules (npm ci restores it); retain useful visual/report artifacts and source. Remove obsolete scratch outputs if helpful.\n5. Mark this log complete with final test counts and artifact paths.\n6. Final chat must include Source Information and all Testing/Engine/Prompt feedback answers, plus the game/interview links. Usage stays \"added on import\"; do not estimate cost.\n\n## Useful commands\nRun inside the source folder:\n- `npm ci`\n- `node tools/build.mjs`\n- `node tools/test.mjs` (one failures-only summary; use --sim, --ui, --hub or --viewports for a tier)\n- `node tools/test.mjs --hub --real` (normal client keyboard co-op path)\n- `node tools/driving-shot.mjs` (1280×720 warmed driving visual)\n- `node tools/shots.mjs` (full art set; heavy on the shared machine)\n\nSource is frozen. No optional feature/polish additions remain planned.\n'\"''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
