overage has passed ≥80% (about 86%).\n- Personally inspected title, daytime/fire/night, map/surgery/mercy and native phone/tablet/landscape/ultrawide screenshots. The warmed driving capture confirms clear forward view, ring steering wheel and handheld map.\n- Product issue tally in docs/issues-log.md: 24 corrected issues, 7 critical. Shared-machine memory kills and test-infrastructure corrections are logged separately.\n\n## Test resources\n- One browser at a time. Full test tiers are separate child processes to release simulation heap.\n- Hub cases use fresh browsers and wait for available RAM; the unmodified official harness is used.\n- Viewport toolkit is wrapped without changing its installed file to serialize native engines/pages.\n- All local servers are OS-selected 127.0.0.1 ports and close automatically. No persistent dev server.\n\n## Remaining hand-in steps\n1. Wait for the current final full test command; fix only an actual failed required check.\n2. Inspect the final result JSON and final source/HTML/interview consistency; original first script must match vendor/session.js.\n3. Run the warmed driving helper only if a final visual refresh is needed, after the test browser closes.\n4. Remove node_modules (npm ci restores it); retain useful visual/report artifacts and source. Remove obsolete scratch outputs if helpful.\n5. Mark this log complete with final test counts and artifact paths.\n6. Final chat must include Source Information and all Testing/Engine/Prompt feedback answers, plus the game/interview links. Usage stays \"added on import\"; do not estimate cost.\n\n## Useful commands\nRun inside the source folder:\n- `npm ci`\n- `node tools/build.mjs`\n- `node tools/test.mjs` (one failures-only summary; use --sim, --ui, --hub or --viewports for a tier)\n- `node tools/test.mjs --hub --real` (normal client keyboard co-op path)\n- `node tools/driving-shot.mjs` (1280×720 warmed driving visual)\n- `node tools/shots.mjs` (full art set; heavy on the shared mach